1
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:16,980
Dark Clouds

2
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:45,200
I'm sorry. I was wrong!

3
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:49,640
I'll apologize for everything!

4
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:51,360
Forgive me.

5
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:55,590
I'll release you.

6
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:57,620
I swear to Odin, I will.

7
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:00,020
Money! I'll even give you money.

8
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,750
I'll give you as much as you want.

9
00:02:05,630 --> 00:02:07,400
That's not enough.

10
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:16,140
It'll take more than that to wipe away
the insults I've suffered until today.

11
00:02:17,970 --> 00:02:21,770
You try being a slave for once.

12
00:02:21,770 --> 00:02:26,870
You won't understand the
depths of my rage otherwise.

13
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:32,520
Okay!

14
00:02:34,490 --> 00:02:37,530
I'll become your slave.

15
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:39,500
I'll serve you.

16
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:45,800
As of today, you'll be the master,
and I'll be the slave.

17
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:50,450
Please, just spare my life, master.

18
00:02:54,110 --> 00:02:58,980
I see. So you'll become my slave.

19
00:02:59,870 --> 00:03:02,930
Yes, gladly.

20
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:12,280
Then whether you live or die...

21
00:03:13,390 --> 00:03:17,240
is up to me.

22
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:44,050
It's been a long time.

23
00:03:45,890 --> 00:03:49,830
Now I must go get her.

24
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:48,000
I guess we won't be visiting
Mister Sverkel to borrow his horse anymore.

25
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:52,730
Why do you look so sullen?

26
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:54,840
I, um...

27
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:58,090
Have you already made your decision?

28
00:05:58,090 --> 00:06:00,050
Huh? About what?

29
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:05,370
What you're going to do once you're free.

30
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:08,020
Oh, that.

31
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:17,300
How would you like to continue working
for me as my retainers once you're free?

32
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:21,620
I'd gladly welcome a couple
of hard workers like you.

33
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:29,240
I know what the master said,
but I don't know.

34
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:32,920
I've lived too long as a slave.

35
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:37,640
I can't make a decision now that
I'm free to choose whatever I want.

36
00:06:38,270 --> 00:06:39,860
That's odd.

37
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:44,790
Does that mean you'd consider staying here?

38
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:51,380
It's true that we don't have a good
relationship with the retainers.

39
00:06:52,690 --> 00:07:00,770
But if I stay here, I might eventually
get a chance to free Arnheid.

40
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:04,890
I'm surprised.

41
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,500
You're that in love with her?

42
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:10,200
Don't. It's not like that.

43
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:14,210
I just...

44
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:18,020
You're taking forever, Gramps!

45
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:19,880
Are you trying to kill me?

46
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:30,550
Where's the old man? He's not with you?

47
00:07:31,530 --> 00:07:33,250
Huh? Oh...

48
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:37,130
The old master isn't back yet?

49
00:07:37,130 --> 00:07:39,760
Not since he left for his farm this morning.

50
00:07:42,380 --> 00:07:47,470
Damn it. It's already time for dinner.

51
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:50,950
He asked us to chop wood for him.

52
00:07:50,950 --> 00:07:55,200
That's odd. Normally he'd be home by now.

53
00:07:56,460 --> 00:08:00,380
I skipped lunch, too. Damn it, Gramps!

54
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:01,780
Are you trying to kill...

55
00:08:04,170 --> 00:08:05,170
Huh?

56
00:08:07,750 --> 00:08:09,700
Where... Where are you going?

57
00:08:10,930 --> 00:08:12,960
To the farm. Follow me.

58
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:15,120
The farm?

59
00:08:37,570 --> 00:08:38,660
Gramps...

60
00:08:41,170 --> 00:08:46,040
Hey, Gramps. Hang in there. Gramps!

61
00:09:28,270 --> 00:09:35,670
So I'm going to die in bed
and not on my farm.

62
00:09:42,030 --> 00:09:44,920
It's open. Let yourself in.

63
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:52,610
Excuse me.

64
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:59,200
The mistress instructed me to come.

65
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:09,520
W-Wow...

66
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:15,950
I-Is there enough here for us, too, Arnheid?

67
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:18,420
Yes.

68
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:22,770
The old master said it would be all right
for me to cook for you as well.

69
00:10:22,770 --> 00:10:25,300
I'm not sure if you'll like it, though.

70
00:10:26,910 --> 00:10:30,310
Oh, I see none of you pray first...

71
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:29,260
So good!

72
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:30,680
Delicious!

73
00:10:31,230 --> 00:10:32,580
It's so good!

74
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:35,770
Master, please have something to eat.

75
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:34,660
This is delicious!

76
00:10:37,580 --> 00:10:41,270
Starting today, I'll be taking care of you.

77
00:10:41,610 --> 00:10:43,680
I'll do anything you ask.

78
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:43,860
So good!

79
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:45,740
Have you had some of this?

80
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:47,740
Will you be staying at my house?

81
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:49,220
Have some of this!

82
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:50,280
What is that?

83
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:53,410
Yes, that's what the mistress told me to do.

84
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:55,700
Is it so good it hurts?

85
00:10:54,590 --> 00:10:55,830
Now eat.

86
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:56,840
You okay?

87
00:10:56,840 --> 00:11:00,580
Let me know if you don't like how it tastes.

88
00:11:03,010 --> 00:11:06,020
I don't need any. I'll eat later.

89
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:08,420
I'm not hungry right now.

90
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,550
Oh, I see.

91
00:11:13,420 --> 00:11:17,220
Don't mind him.
Just shove the spoon in his mouth.

92
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:17,970
What?

93
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:23,820
Gramps is just embarrassed about being fed.

94
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:25,900
Get used to it, Gramps.

95
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:31,000
Until you've recovered,
you're going to be fed for a while.

96
00:11:32,930 --> 00:11:34,840
Did you just laugh?

97
00:11:35,810 --> 00:11:37,160
N-No.

98
00:11:38,340 --> 00:11:41,770
I'm really not hungry. I'll eat later—

99
00:11:57,440 --> 00:12:00,120
Get out of here!

100
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:13,050
I'll wash the dishes.

101
00:12:13,050 --> 00:12:15,200
No, I'll do it.

102
00:12:19,170 --> 00:12:24,500
I'm glad the old master seems to be
doing better than I'd heard.

103
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:29,080
And he doesn't seem as scary as they say.

104
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:33,610
Yeah. He's actually a kind man at heart.

105
00:12:33,610 --> 00:12:35,470
He can be scary sometimes, though.

106
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:39,600
I think I know what you mean.

107
00:12:40,690 --> 00:12:41,380
Hmph.

108
00:12:42,850 --> 00:12:43,780
But...

109
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:57,140
I haven't had so much fun
at a meal in a long time.

110
00:12:57,140 --> 00:12:58,740
Neither have I.

111
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:06,680
It was like I was free again.

112
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:15,110
You're right. It did feel like that.

113
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,970
Hey, slaves. Is Snake around?

114
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:42,070
A runaway slave?

115
00:13:43,060 --> 00:13:47,420
Yeah. He escaped from
Kjallakr's farm three days ago.

116
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:51,490
That Kjallakr, huh?

117
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:56,440
He's always treated his slaves poorly.

118
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:58,050
He got what he deserved.

119
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:02,220
Actually, it's not that simple.

120
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:08,840
The slave killed Kjallakr and his sons
and set his house on fire.

121
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:12,900
He's a violent man and a skilled fighter.

122
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:21,540
Kjallakr's uncle said he'd give three
horses to whoever catches him.

123
00:14:21,980 --> 00:14:23,810
What should we do, boss?

124
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:30,400
The three horses aside,
we should probably take precautions.

125
00:14:32,010 --> 00:14:37,380
Keep watch in groups of three for a while.

126
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:43,830
Even if you spot him,
don't try too hard to catch him.

127
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:46,530
Call for reinforcements first.

128
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:55,300
There's no telling
what a cornered man will do.

129
00:15:42,820 --> 00:15:44,550
Look. That's him.

130
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:48,700
That's his hilt catching the sun.

131
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:52,780
Is he sleeping?

132
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:58,280
Looks like it. Just based on appearances,
he looks like a beggar or pilgrim.

133
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:00,550
He looks pretty suspicious, right?

134
00:16:00,950 --> 00:16:02,880
Yeah, sure does.

135
00:16:03,220 --> 00:16:06,980
Hey, keep your voices down.

136
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:08,650
Does that mean it's him?

137
00:16:08,650 --> 00:16:10,930
The guy worth three horses...

138
00:16:10,930 --> 00:16:13,220
Yeah, it's gotta be.

139
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:13,960
Hey.

140
00:16:14,700 --> 00:16:16,790
It's our lucky day.

141
00:16:16,790 --> 00:16:19,210
You idiot, you can't assume that.

142
00:16:18,770 --> 00:16:21,330
Hey, keep your voices down.

143
00:16:19,210 --> 00:16:19,690
Huh?

144
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:22,180
Isn't he supposed to be pretty tough?

145
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:27,000
We'll be fine. We'll bag him easily
while he's still asleep.

146
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:27,000
Guys, keep your voices down.

147
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,790
We should call for help, like the boss said.

148
00:16:30,090 --> 00:16:32,180
Don't be a wuss, Lizard.

149
00:16:32,180 --> 00:16:35,320
If we call for help,
we'll get smaller shares.

150
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:38,420
I told you to keep your voices down.

151
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:42,360
How are you so confident when we
don't even know how strong he is?

152
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:44,040
The reward is horses.

153
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:48,650
If we catch him now,
each of us gets a whole horse.

154
00:16:48,650 --> 00:16:50,630
It's not gonna go that well.

155
00:16:50,630 --> 00:16:53,180
Keep your voices down.

156
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:55,460
There's nothing wrong with butchering a horse
and cooking a leg or two to eat, fatty.

157
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:56,970
What was that, you shrimp?

158
00:16:56,970 --> 00:16:59,140
If you're so desperate to die,
go die by yourself.

159
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:01,110
I'll kill you first.

160
00:17:01,110 --> 00:17:03,300
Not if I kill you first.

161
00:17:02,050 --> 00:17:05,750
Keep your voices down, idiots.

162
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:04,890
Bring it on.

163
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:38,710
Man, it's hot.

164
00:17:48,770 --> 00:17:49,640
Okay.

165
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:57,750
Thorfinn, I've got a lot of
chopped wood waiting here.

166
00:17:58,020 --> 00:17:59,940
Keep 'em moving.

167
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:04,470
Hey, Thorfinn.

168
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:10,120
S-Sorry, one second.

169
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,160
Sure thing.

170
00:18:15,380 --> 00:18:18,230
What is Thorfinn doing?

171
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:22,770
Snake is reading the Bible inside.

172
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:28,070
The old master can't read himself.
Thorfinn's eavesdropping on them.

173
00:18:28,070 --> 00:18:32,990
I see. So Thorfinn is a Christian, too.

174
00:18:33,530 --> 00:18:39,000
No, but he says it's interesting.

175
00:18:42,430 --> 00:18:51,190
"You have heard that it was said, 'You shall
love your neighbor and hate your enemy.'"

176
00:18:51,800 --> 00:19:00,880
"But I say to you, love your enemies and
pray for those who persecute you,"

177
00:19:02,050 --> 00:19:05,900
"so that you may be sons of
your Father who is in heaven;"

178
00:19:06,420 --> 00:19:11,410
"for He causes His sun
to rise on the evil and the good,"

179
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:18,200
"and sends rain on the righteous
and the unrighteous."

180
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:27,720
"For if you love those who love you,
what reward do you have?"

181
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:33,970
"Do not even the tax collectors do the same?"

182
00:19:34,430 --> 00:19:42,020
"If you greet only your brothers,
what more are you doing than others?"

183
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:47,440
"Do not even the Gentiles do the same?"

184
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:57,800
"Therefore you are to be perfect,
as your heavenly Father is perfect."

185
00:19:58,460 --> 00:20:01,720
Good grief, that's ridiculous.

186
00:20:02,490 --> 00:20:05,930
Gramps, I'm sick of the Gospel.

187
00:20:05,930 --> 00:20:07,620
Let's read the first bit again.

188
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:09,460
It's more interesting than this, at least.

189
00:20:12,450 --> 00:20:15,240
Hey, Gramps, what are you doing?

190
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:16,370
Going for a piss?

191
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:20,060
The... The wheat...

192
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:24,550
I must harvest the wheat.

193
00:20:26,050 --> 00:20:30,740
I told you, they finished
the harvest a while ago.

194
00:20:30,740 --> 00:20:32,320
Stay in bed.

195
00:20:35,780 --> 00:20:37,250
Arnheid!

196
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:40,160
Gramps pissed himself. Do you mind?

197
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:41,450
Got it.

198
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,090
I'll help, too.

199
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,470
He's gone senile.

200
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:58,850
He probably doesn't have much longer to live.

201
00:20:59,270 --> 00:20:59,900
What?

202
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:00,600
What?

203
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:06,520
But he's well enough to go out
on the farm every day.

204
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:10,230
Yeah, and he always goes fishing
a couple times a day.

205
00:21:10,710 --> 00:21:13,260
But he's old enough to have great-grandkids.

206
00:21:13,260 --> 00:21:16,960
Old folks suddenly lose all their strength
once their legs start to go.

207
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:21,200
But it won't be right away.

208
00:21:21,590 --> 00:21:26,120
You guys should repay his kindness
while you still have the chance.

209
00:21:29,490 --> 00:21:33,460
There's something I've been wondering.

210
00:21:33,940 --> 00:21:38,300
What's your relationship with the old master?

211
00:21:38,630 --> 00:21:43,180
Huh? It's nothing special.

212
00:21:44,620 --> 00:21:50,200
I'm just planning to inherit and sell
that book once Gramps kicks the bucket.

213
00:21:54,520 --> 00:21:58,790
Get back to work. The sun's setting.

214
00:21:58,790 --> 00:21:59,730
Right.

215
00:22:18,090 --> 00:22:19,080
Ow!

216
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:22,180
Ouch...

217
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:48,580
He's riding fast.

218
00:22:48,580 --> 00:22:50,050
Is it one of my men?

219
00:22:51,420 --> 00:22:53,000
No...

220
00:22:53,380 --> 00:22:55,880
Hey, you on the horse. Stop!

221
00:22:57,020 --> 00:22:59,260
Boss!

222
00:23:00,570 --> 00:23:04,510
That's him! The runaway slave!

223
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:09,020
He killed Lizard! Get him!

224
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:11,900
Seriously? Damn it.

225
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:14,270
My sword's inside the house.

226
00:23:16,140 --> 00:23:17,040
It can't be...

227
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:27,290
Gardar!

228
00:23:41,660 --> 00:23:43,060
Arnheid!

229
00:23:48,850 --> 00:23:51,190
I've finally found you,

230
00:23:52,110 --> 00:23:54,080
my wife!

231
00:25:36,830 --> 00:25:40,210
Freedom

232
00:25:38,040 --> 00:25:39,190
"Freedom."
